From: Boot Time Experiment <boot-time@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm: k3: defer J7200 Falcon core1 cleanup to TF-A

Do not send MCU core1 cleanup requests from the boot R5 host.
The paired Falcon TF-A change performs the sequence on A72.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [J7200 Falcon experiment]

--- a/arch/arm/mach-k3/common.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-k3/common.c
@@ -744,12 +744,7 @@
 	if (ret)
 		panic("%s: Failed to boot in falcon mode: %d\n", __func__, ret);
 
-	/* A72 SPL normally performs this J7200 split-mode housekeeping. */
-	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_TARGET_J7200_R5_EVM)) {
-		ret = shutdown_mcu_r5_core1();
-		if (ret)
-			panic("Unable to shutdown MCU R5 core 1, %d\n", ret);
-	}
+	/* J7200 core1 cleanup runs on A72 in the Falcon TF-A build. */
 #endif
 #if !(defined(CONFIG_SYS_ICACHE_OFF) && defined(CONFIG_SYS_DCACHE_OFF))
 	dcache_disable();
